   "q_en": "<p>A train passes a station 1050 m long in 48 seconds at a 126 km/hr speed. Find the time taken by the train to pass an electric pole. </p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; 126 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 1050 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2358;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 48 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2346;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "25 seconds",
    "28 seconds",
    "20 seconds",
    "30 seconds"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;",
    "28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;",
    "20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;",
    "30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"
   ],
   "answer": 2,
   "solution_en": "<p>Let the length of the train be 'l' m.</p><p>Speed of train = 126 * 5/18 = 35 m/s</p><p>Time = distance/ speed </p><p>50 seconds = (1050 + l)/ 35</p><p>1050 + l = 1750</p><p>l = 700</p><p>time taken by the train to pass an electric pole = 700/ 35 = 20 seconds</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length of the train be 'l' m.</p><p>Speed of train = 126 * 5/18 = 35 m/s</p><p>Time = distance/ speed </p><p>50 seconds = (1050 + l)/ 35</p><p>1050 + l = 1750</p><p>l = 700</p><p>time taken by the train to pass an electric pole = 700/ 35 = 20 seconds</p>",
